updated_at: "2026-10-23T23:02:31.051Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "F03: reverse blocks and unresolved prerequisites are held with blocker evidence until resolved; F05: custom terminal roles are excluded and custom active statuses remain eligible across brief lifecycle views; F14: multilingual brief delta and divergence budgets use SDK UTF-8 estimates for exact output"
comments[24]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T20:25:08.967Z",codex-agent,"Verified F03 F05 F14 against origin/main cdcd1e3: outgoing-only active-ID blockers miss reverse blocks and missing targets, lifecycle helpers hard-code spellings, and both estimators divide UTF-16 length by four. All findings valid. The pinned SDK exports runtime status and UTF-8 estimation helpers plus blocker resolution; preserve legacy depends_on aliases at the SDK boundary. Owner explicitly groups these findings in one PR."
  "2026-10-23T20:33:07.947Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses public isTerminalStatus (the SDK alias-normalizing terminal-role wrapper), resolveRuntimeStatusRegistry/readSettings, indexBlockedByIds plus resolveItemBlockers, and estimatePmOutputTokens. Published minimum SDK 2026.10.13 exports all imports, so dev/peer and manifest floors remain unchanged. Preserve depends_on as a blocker alias and external source provenance. Divergence classification has no lifecycle predicate, while delta transitions and duplicate remediation now receive the workspace registry. Focused native non-git regressions pass 4/4; pm-linked run passed 3/3 before the external-provenance case was added."
  "2026-10-23T20:39:54.269Z",codex-agent,"Isolated behavioural revert proofs after rebuilding: F03 reverting only blockerRelationships fails F03 at reverse blocks must hold A (exit 1). F05 restoring only legacy isClosed/isClosedStatus bodies fails F05 because accepted and the accepted Decision return to next candidates (exit 1). F14 reverting only estimateTokens and measureRenderedBrief to UTF-16 length fails F14 at the emitted-byte ceiling (exit 1). Each proof ran node --test --test-name-pattern=<finding>: test/sdk-semantics.test.ts after npm run build. Restored all functions and rebuilt. Final lifecycle helper uses the named statusIsTerminal SDK export. Existing optional local strict-health warnings are extension host skew and merge_fence_drift:2 tracked by pm-brief-fence165, with history_drift clean. No fence or history repair is in scope."
  "2026-10-23T21:02:47.341Z",codex-agent,"Clean-identity npm run release:check passed: 429 tests, 0 failures, 0 skipped; coverage 100.00 percent lines, 98.11 percent branches, 100.00 percent functions across all 4 production sources at unchanged thresholds. Packed acceptance passed npm-current and bun-current on SDK 2026.10.20 plus npm-minimum on SDK 2026.10.13, each with typed cannot-fit exit 2. Changelog and publish-attestation checks passed. Clean-identity bun run release:check is running. Preparing a draft PR so remote CI can run concurrently."
  "2026-10-23T21:05:45.603Z",codex-agent,"Draft PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/pull/173 opened with finding evidence and the requested main-path item link. Remote CI is running. DeepScan reports one new static issue and inspection found an unused root binding in the new regression file. Removed that binding and its sole import dependency without changing production code or test assertions. Test compilation passes; awaiting the refreshed static check. Local npm release gate is green and the full Bun gate continues."
  "2026-10-23T21:13:27.563Z",codex-agent,"Final local validation: clean-identity npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed 429/429 tests, 0 failures, 0 skipped. All 4 production sources reported: npm coverage lines/branches/functions 100.00/98.11/100.00 percent; Bun 100.00/98.07/100.00 percent. Thresholds unchanged at 100/97.85/100. Packed npm-current, bun-current and npm-minimum acceptance passed 3/3 in each gate, including minimum SDK 2026.10.13. Changelog and publish-attestation checks passed. Final pm-linked node --test test/sdk-semantics.test.ts passed 4/4. Repeated isolated rebuild/revert proofs: F03 fails reverse blocks must hold A; F05 fails accepted-item exclusion; F14 fails json: 490 exceeds 441. All three exit 1 under their isolated revert and pass after restoration; restored source matches the committed file exactly."
  "2026-10-23T21:13:31.690Z",codex-agent,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/pull/173 is verified at code head 4cc9cacf9dc55d30e489c96208d2a38576a3ed84: CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/actions/runs/40024255385 passed all 5 jobs (npm and Bun release gates, Node 22 and 26 tests, Windows audit); CodeQL, Semgrep, DeepScan and Hound passed. DeepScan cleared after the unused fixture binding cleanup. CodeRabbit skipped the draft and is not review approval. Final receipt commit will receive fresh CI. Findings F03/F05/F14 are all valid and fixed, no dependency or manifest bump required. Releasing the claim while retaining in_progress for orchestrator verification; no merge or release performed. Existing optional local strict-health fence/skew warnings remain outside this change and are documented above."
  "2026-10-23T21:34:06.213Z",codex-agent,"PR 173 review round: remote branch is current and includes main. GraphQL returned zero review threads; no CodeRabbit review body exists and its issue comment reports automatic review skipped. Independent verdict is valid: external reverse blocks collide with local IDs. Audit blocker indexing, context orientation, relationship deduplication and dependent scoring for external/local identity isolation, with native non-git regressions and isolated behavioral revert proofs."
  "2026-10-23T21:36:56.372Z",codex-agent,"Implemented external/local namespace isolation in reverse indexing, context reversal and incoming context links, active-dependent ranking counts, and relationship deduplication/self-ID handling. Focused suite passes 9/9 with real plain-directory trackers for global/external reverse edges and direct external blockers plus local controls. The pinned SDK indexBlockedByIds ignores reverse-edge provenance; adapted its input locally without dependency changes. Four isolated function revert proofs are running before full clean-identity npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-23T21:37:32.176Z",codex-agent,"Four isolated behavioral reverts, each rebuilding before node --test --test-name-pattern=<pattern> test/sdk-semantics.test.ts, all exited 1: blockerRelationships with pattern external reverse isolation: global fails external reverse edge must not block local A; toBriefItem with the same pattern fails empty local dependency context; activeDependentCount with pattern external context isolation: fails 2 !== 1; extractRelationships with pattern external identity isolation: fails 1 !== 3. Each revert replaced only that function from the pre-review HEAD. Fixed source restored after every proof and rebuilt. Whole PR diff reviewed for provenance leakage in blocker resolution, risk output, ranking, context links and identity handling; all matching sites addressed. New regressions cover global, external alias, URI references, genuine local controls, external/local collisions and external self-ID targets."
  "2026-10-23T22:00:25.248Z",codex-agent,"Review baseline aaa2f18. Restored source and tracker-linked regression run pass 9/9. Clean-identity npm release gate coverage passes 434/434 tests, 0 failures, 0 skipped/cancelled, with all 4 production sources reported at 100.00 percent lines, 98.08 percent branches, 100.00 percent functions; thresholds remain 100/97.85/100. Production audit and package dry run pass. Packed acceptance is running from its isolated tarball, after its final build, so the clean-identity Bun gate can now run independently without concurrent generated-file writes. No timeouts or retries so far."
  "2026-10-23T22:08:43.836Z",codex-agent,"Full clean-identity npm run release:check exited 0: 434 tests passed, 0 failed/skipped/cancelled; all 4 sources meet unchanged thresholds at 100.00/98.08/100.00 percent lines/branches/functions. Packed acceptance passed 3/3: npm-current and bun-current on SDK 2026.10.20, npm-minimum on SDK 2026.10.13. Production audit reports 0 vulnerabilities; changelog check and publish-attestation verification pass. No timeouts or retries. Final self-review clarified only the deduplication comment, preserving executable code and line count; Bun gate remains running and will rebuild the final package."
  "2026-10-23T22:14:26.424Z",codex-agent,"Bun first attempt passed all 434 tests with 0 failed/skipped/cancelled, but the line coverage gate failed at 99.83 percent (branches 98.12, functions 100). A two-line source-comment clarification occurred while instrumented processes were running, changing byte offsets without changing executable code or line count. That can invalidate merged V8 coverage offsets, so this is not a valid final coverage measurement. No thresholds or tests changed; source is now frozen and a full clean-identity Bun release gate retry is running. This was not a timeout. Preserve the failed attempt and report the retry outcome explicitly."
  "2026-10-23T22:25:04.667Z",codex-agent,"Final validation: npm run release:check and the frozen-source bun run release:check retry both exit 0 with 434/434 tests, 0 failed/skipped/cancelled, and all 4 production sources reported. Npm coverage lines/branches/functions is 100.00/98.08/100.00 percent; Bun is 100.00/98.12/100.00 percent, at unchanged 100/97.85/100 thresholds. Both gates pass packed acceptance 3/3 (npm-current, bun-current, npm-minimum), production audit with 0 vulnerabilities, changelog validation and publish-attestation verification. The first Bun attempt passed 434 tests but failed line coverage at 99.83 percent after a comment edit during instrumentation; the complete retry with frozen hashes passes. No timeout occurred. Four isolated function revert proofs remain documented above; focused and pm-linked suite passed 9/9. Fresh GitHub fetch returns zero review threads and no CodeRabbit review body; automated review remains unavailable. SDK gap encountered: indexBlockedByIds drops external reverse-edge provenance, guarded locally without a pin change. Releasing the claim and retaining in_progress for orchestrator verification; no replies, thread resolution, merge or release."
  "2026-10-23T22:33:20.759Z",codex-agent,"Review round: remote head is current and includes main. GraphQL enumerated all review threads (zero unresolved); paginated reviews contain no CodeRabbit review or Outside diff range findings. Verified second read-only verdict: restore default done terminal semantics, pass workspace status roles into native disclosure, and isolate local/global same-ID direct blocker resolution. Preserve existing reverse-edge external isolation. Add native non-git table-driven relationship/readiness tests and behavioral revert proofs, then unchanged npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-23T22:38:51.250Z",codex-agent,"Self-review found two further instances: imported local self blockers were discarded, and active dependency counts collapsed same-ID local/external resources. Both now fail closed and retain namespace identity. Added 152 native non-git relationship cases covering blocks, blocked_by, parent, related, legacy depends_on; implicit/explicit local, global/external; open/terminal/missing/self/cycle/duplicate/collision targets; URI references and scalar blocked_by including the no-active-blocker sentinel. Fixtures use SDK serialization and certified complete reads; import-only self/duplicate shapes bypass mutation restrictions only in disposable trackers. Initial URI fixture writes required allowUnresolvedDeps under the pinned SDK; adjusted fixture setup without changing production behavior."
  "2026-10-23T22:40:45.484Z",codex-agent,"Seven isolated behavioral revert proofs passed (each npm run build then node --test --test-name-pattern=<pattern> <file>, each reverted run exited 1 with AssertionError): (1) restore HEAD isClosedStatus, pattern ^B1: includes completed done in next; (2) restore HEAD blockerRelationships, ^B1: keeps done prerequisites blocked; (3) restore HEAD buildDisclosureBrief, ^B2: recommends accepted work; (4) restore HEAD blockerRelationships, ^B3: loses local title/status evidence for both global/external collisions; (5) restore HEAD extractRelationships, matrix blocks/implicit-local/self: recommends self-blocked work; (6) restore HEAD activeDependencyCount, matrix blocked_by/implicit-local/collision: loses distinct namespace count; (7) remove only local reverse-index provenance guard in blockerRelationships, external reverse isolation: global: local namesake incorrectly blocked. All functions restored in finally and rebuilt; the preceding fixed focused run passed 165/165. Original F03/F05/F14 revert proofs remain above. No review threads were replied to or resolved."
  "2026-10-23T22:41:23.425Z",codex-agent,"After restoring all revert proofs, pm test pm-brief-agze --run --progress passed both linked commands: node --test test/sdk-semantics.test.ts (13/13) and node --test test/relationship-shapes.test.ts (152/152), with all failure categories zero. Source is frozen for full clean-identity release gates at unchanged thresholds. SDK compatibility observations: default runtime registry omits legacy done; reverse index drops provenance; direct blocker resolver conflates local/global same-ID references; URI fixture writes require explicit unresolved-dependency allowance. No upstream reports filed in this round."
  "2026-10-23T22:41:48.114Z",codex-agent,Whole-diff review also restored the pre-PR momentum fixture status done in test/brief.test.ts. The earlier done-to-closed fixture edit masked the legacy compatibility regression; the original behavioral coverage now remains intact alongside B1. Candidate implementation commit is 06312f3. Full gates will run after this final test restoration.
  "2026-10-23T22:43:53.033Z",codex-agent,"The first full npm gate attempt exposed a stale existing adapter expectation: test/brief.test.ts expected an imported depends_on self-reference to be discarded. Updated its exact extracted relationship and eight-entry context assertions to retain the self blocker, matching the intentional fail-closed contract exercised by the matrix. The targeted adapter test now passes 1/1. Production source remains unchanged. This is an assertion-expectation correction, not a timeout or a threshold change; a complete clean-identity gate retry will follow."
  "2026-10-23T22:52:26.852Z",codex-agent,"Resumed after orchestration interruption: worktree clean at 6010dea with the existing item still claimed and in_progress. Remote PR head unchanged; branch includes main. The initial npm gate finished with 589/590 tests passing and only the now-corrected legacy self-edge adapter expectation failing. No timeouts, skips or cancellations. Seven revert proofs and the 165/165 focused results remain recorded; they were not repeated. A full clean-identity npm release gate retry is now running on the final committed source and tests."
  "2026-10-23T22:56:38.604Z",codex-agent,"Clean-identity npm retry passed 590/590 tests, zero failed/skipped/cancelled; coverage 100.00/98.22/100.00 percent lines/branches/functions across all four production sources at unchanged thresholds. Production audit and package dry run pass. Installed-tarball acceptance has passed the source-build/pack boundary and is running solely in disposable projects. Starting the clean-identity Bun gate now; no remaining npm step writes shared build or coverage outputs, and production source/tests remain frozen. Revert restores refer to review-start head 5eced77de033ece6febd6edf19da8c08701686ad."
  "2026-10-23T22:58:11.542Z",codex-agent,"Full clean-identity npm run release:check retry exited 0 on code/test head 6010dea: 590/590 tests, zero failed/skipped/cancelled; all four production sources reported at 100.00/98.22/100.00 percent lines/branches/functions. Packed acceptance passed 3/3 (npm-current and bun-current SDK 2026.10.20; npm-minimum SDK 2026.10.13), including native disclosure in all audiences and cannot-fit exit 2. Audit: zero vulnerabilities. Changelog and publish-attestation verification passed. No timeouts occurred. The complete clean-identity Bun gate is still running."
  "2026-10-23T23:02:30.319Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round validation: clean-identity npm run release:check retry and bun run release:check both exited 0 on code/test head 6010dea. Each passed 590/590 tests, zero failed/skipped/cancelled, with all four production sources at 100.00/98.22/100.00 percent lines/branches/functions; thresholds remain 100/97.85/100. Each passed packed acceptance 3/3 (npm-current, bun-current, npm-minimum), audit with zero vulnerabilities, changelog and publish-attestation verification. No timeouts. First npm attempt was 589/590 because the existing adapter assertion still discarded self-dependencies; corrected exact assertions passed on full retry. Seven isolated rebuild-and-revert proofs each exited 1, restored focused suites passed 165/165, and both linked pm tests passed (13 plus 152 cases). All second-verdict findings are valid and fixed, the first reverse-isolation blocker stays fixed, and the matrix covers every requested kind/provenance/graph shape. No unresolved GitHub thread IDs or CodeRabbit review body existed on complete rereads. Independent automated review remains unavailable (CodeRabbit skipped, Greptile trial ended); this is missing evidence. SDK default-done, reverse provenance and direct-namespace collision gaps are adapted locally; URI mutation validation needs explicit unresolved allowance in fixtures. No upstream issues filed. Rebuilt dist remains ignored; pins and floors unchanged. Commits 06312f3, c0187bf, 6010dea include code/tests and append-only tracker evidence. Release claim for orchestrator verification; retain in_progress. No thread reply/resolution, merge or release performed."
